# Phase-critic Colab round (PC, STANCE7): result

2026-11-02 (UTC). Six 12M-step training runs on Colab L4 runtimes; report only; nothing merged. The reading is the
pinned scorer's (score_pc.py 3c55bf21, run 19:12:31-19:12:44 UTC). The flagged deviation reading is the approved
deviation tool's (score_pc_dev.py efb37b20, run 19:13:15-19:13:22 UTC). Two independent checks found no wrong number
and no blocking process problem. They also found that the three switch-off runs are bit-for-bit copies of last week's
STANCE6 runs. [measured] cites a file and line or field; [inferred] marks reasoning.

Short names. ST = /home/user/work/pc_study. RUNLOG = S1/foot/stance4/live/run_log.txt; S1 and S2 are the two
scratchpad folders that ST/round/criteria.txt lines 38-40 define. RUNLOG was read at 971 lines (sha256 89425ea9...);
the scorers read it at 966 lines (8c05d9ba...). `<prefix>/` stands for the agent branch prefix, left out under the rule
against product names. PHASE = the three runs with the phase input; OFF = the three switch-off runs.

